  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nCold front shifts east of the area this morning and drier air \nmoves over the region for today. The area of low pressure \nstationed across the Mid-Atlantic Coast and across the Great \nLakes could bring some light showers later this afternoon and \nevening, but best chances appear to stay west/east of the area \nat this time. Chances for rain increase again for this weekend, \nas an upper level low moves over central NY on Saturday. This \nsystem will bring periods of rain rain showers right through \nSunday morning. There will be a brief lull in shower activity on\nSunday and then another upper trough dips down across the \nregion and brings additional rain chances Sunday night into \nMonday. A slight reprieve from wet conditions appear possible \nlate Monday through Wednesday, before an unsettled pattern takes\nhold of the region towards the end of the week.",
